    "updated_at": "2026-11-15T14:44:54Z",
    "body": "Claim released. The quick gate failed twice.\n\nBoth failures also occur with unchanged upstream/main at 8719d8b7a028f0c93cc78fe32ccbfdf5297a0dca:\n\n- detect_holes_note_tests::detect_holes_on_a_bore_op_with_only_a_wide_hole_is_refused stores 1 hole. The test expects 0.\n- detect_holes_note_tests::detect_holes_on_a_bore_op_stores_the_small_hole_and_names_the_wide_one stores 2 holes. The test expects 1.\n\nThe source diff was empty during the upstream reproduction. The fix does not change either UI test or hole detection.\n\nThe local implementation adds bounded 3D edge-break volumes, profile persistence, frame rotation, and simulation credit. All 16 new tests pass. All 8 legacy edge-break tests pass. All 28 mutation checks fail with the mutation and pass after restoration. The domain and app gate suites pass. Clippy passes for all touched crates and for the gate retry.\n\nDecisions: Keep legacy cone records unchanged. Add optional framed volumes with a zero slope, so older readers discard them safely. Bound their depth by their width, and their width by the operation. Credit only connected declared material below the model surface. Keep full-precision 3D endpoints to preserve frame orthogonality. Use normalized circle intersections to preserve small sagittas and very small direction rates. Replacing all legacy records and using projected XY distance were rejected because they break compatibility or lose 3D bounds.\n\nThe staged, uncommitted work remains on local branch issue/1891-edge-break-volumes in .claude/worktrees/issue-1891 on len. No commit or PR was created. No golden files changed.\n\nLocal evidence: /tmp/1891-red.log, /tmp/1891-mutations-summary.txt, /tmp/1891-upstream-ui-baseline.log, and /tmp/1891-gate-retry.log.\n",
